@startuml mw_log_dynamic_design

participant "Application\nThread" as App
participant "DataRouterRecorder" as DRR
participant "DataRouterBackend" as DRB
participant "SharedMemoryWriter" as SMW
participant "AlternatingControlBlock\n(shared memory)" as ACB
participant "DatarouterMessageClientImpl\nbackground thread" as BG
participant "MessagePassingServer\n(daemon)" as MPS

note over App, ACB
  Hot path — entirely wait-free on the application thread
end note

App -> DRR : StartRecord(context_id, level)
DRR -> DRB : ReserveSlot()
DRB --> DRR : SlotHandle (from CircularAllocator)
DRR --> App : SlotHandle

App -> DRR : Log(slot, value) [repeats for each value]
note right of DRR : Serialize value into LogRecord in slot

App -> DRR : StopRecord(slot)
DRR -> DRB : FlushSlot(slot)
DRB -> SMW : AllocAndWrite(timestamp, type_id, size, callback)

alt buffer full (active LinearControlBlock has no remaining capacity)
  SMW -> SMW : increment number_of_drops_buffer_full\nand size_of_drops_buffer_full in SharedData
  SMW --> DRB : return (no write, no block)
else oversized payload (> 65,500 bytes)
  SMW -> SMW : increment number_of_drops_invalid_size in SharedData
  SMW --> DRB : return (no write)
else capacity available
  SMW -> ACB : WaitFreeAlternatingWriter::Acquire(size)\n— increment number_of_writers (register-before-reserve)\n— fetch_add acquired_index to reserve bytes
  ACB --> SMW : span<byte> in active buffer
  SMW -> ACB : copy BufferEntryHeader + serialized LogRecord bytes
  SMW -> ACB : WaitFreeAlternatingWriter::Release()\n— release fence → written_index.fetch_add()\n— decrement number_of_writers (last)
  note right of ACB
    No mutex taken. All atomics seq_cst.
    Release ordering: fence → written_index
    → number_of_writers (last) ensures
    reader gate not unblocked prematurely.
  end note
  SMW --> DRB : done
end

DRB --> DRR : done
DRR --> App : done

note over BG, MPS
  Background path — IPC runs independently of the application thread.
  Daemon polls PeekNumberOfBytesAcquiredInBuffer; when data is ready,
  it sends kAcquireRequest to the client.
end note

MPS -> BG : kAcquireRequest\n(daemon requests buffer switch)
BG -> ACB : SharedMemoryWriter::ReadAcquire()\n— OnAcquireRequest() handler:\n  AlternatingReaderProxy::Switch():\n  resets opposite block, increments switch_count\n— returns ReadAcquireResult{acquired_buffer}
ACB --> BG : ReadAcquireResult
BG -> MPS : kAcquireResponse(ReadAcquireResult)\n(OnAcquireResponse stores in data_acquired)

note over MPS, ACB
  Next Tick():
end note
MPS -> ACB : SharedMemoryReader::IsBlockReleasedByWriters(block_count)\n— Phase 1: TryFinalizeAcquisition()\n— polls until number_of_writers==0\n  AND written_index==acquired_index\n— acquire fence on true
ACB --> MPS : gate cleared
MPS -> MPS : SharedMemoryReader::NotifyAcquisitionSetReader(acquire_result)\n— sets up reader for acquired buffer
MPS -> MPS : SharedMemoryReader::Read(on_new_type, on_new_record)\n— Phase 2: ProcessAndRouteLogMessages()\n— on_new_type → AddIncomingType()\n— on_new_record → ParseSharedMemoryRecord()\n  → dispatch to DltLogServer via IOutput

@enduml
